description:
Assist Project Manager to implement and monitor of environmental management systems (including vector control, earth control measures) at work sites.


To look out for conditions/ situations in construction site which causes environmental health problems or are likely to cause environmental health problems and report to the Project Manager of the construction site together with recommendations on remedial measures to be taken to prevent recurrence;


Ensure environmental compliance


Prepare and submit a Site Environmental Control Programme to the Project Manager of the construction site


Inspect the construction site to ensure all facilities and equipment are relevant to the maintenance of environmental health are in proper working condition and do not pose any environmental health hazard;


Point out and discuss environmental health irregularities such as mosquito and fly breeding, rodent infestation, noise/dust/smoke/water pollution, poor housekeeping, earth littering, poor refuse management, poor maintenance of sanitary facilities, etc. with the Project Manager of the construction site and recommend measures to rectify such irregularities;


Attend to all feedback on such irregularities and inform the Project Manager of the construction site accordingly;


Report and submit a Site Environmental Control Report to the Project Manager of the construction site once every fortnightly;


Assist the authorities to investigate outbreaks of infectious, vector-borne or food-borne diseases on the construction site;


Organise campaigns, training courses and other activities to develop and sustain the interest of workers in maintaining good environmental health standards in the construction site; and


Be responsible for any other duties that may be assigned to you from time to time as your superior/management deem fit.


Possess at least a technician diploma from an acceptable polytechnic relevant Degree


At least 1-2 years of relevant work experience in construction field (Preferable in LTA Projects)


NEA registered Environmental Control Officer (ECO).


Proficient in Excel, PPT & Word


6 working days


Immediate position available ; Preferable short notice / immediate candidate


**Interested applicants kindly submit your resume included :** Current & expected salary and reson for leaving current company


CHUAN LIM CONSTRUCTION PTE LTD
